**Status — implemented, verification pending (2026-11-15).** Changed-input filtering, linear bulk metric traversal, existing resolver reuse and changed-only control writes are implemented. This task no longer asks for another dirty journal or a duplicate style cache. Authored-item maintenance now shares its recovery snapshot, borrows definitions and applies only differing live style/geometry fields; AUTHORING-VERIFY in Overhaul.md owns its lifecycle, validation, serialization and total-cost checks. Repeated full state copies and whole-part lookups are no longer pending implementation. Shared component reference collection also uses one output buffer through nested parts, including mutable-reference consumers, and rebinding prepares declared keys once. AUTHORING-VERIFY covers those ordered-reference and backend-consumer contracts.

**Still to verify:** Check first creation, explicit writes, reparenting, reset/zero values, theme changes and unrelated caret/text changes before same-tick consumers. Account for scanning and invalidation maintenance as well as avoided writes.

**Why:** Cheap steady reads must remain correct when a real style dependency changes.

**Current instruction:** source changes only. Do not run checks, compile, measure, ship or restart from this Record. Use [Overhaul.md](Overhaul.md#remaining-acceptance-obligations) and [the checkpoint](record:r_2KDK4ZZZJNBEK0J23TFNQAZF9Y); verification resumes only when authorized. Quantity remains zero because implementation is not a performance pass.
} r_6TZTP766V7XVXM52YEHB3EMJKZ

