P80 — Verify dormant camera-image retention. (
    @park-p80: 0,
    is #task,
    #park-performance-task,
    #park-stage-a1,
    #part-of @park-dev-04-style-layout-and-retention: 55,
    #park-workflow @park-development-cycle
) { r_4MPVWB5R7J40MNV571W780DQ9W
**Current workflow:** [Development cycle](record:r_043BC6V4K9R3X6E9E4TZP3P6J0). **Resume state:** [Current checkpoint](record:r_2KDK4ZZZJNBEK0J23TFNQAZF9Y).

**Implementation is complete for the dormant-camera case; verification only.** The source-only capture-write receipt in [Overhaul.md](Overhaul.md) records encoded-write revisions and a single current-writer/dependency table. An image with known inactive camera writers can retain its containing capture until its content revision, texture identity, CPU asset or other visual input changes. Active cameras, storage textures, unknown/removed writers and filtered capture keep conservative invalidation. Provenance seeding cannot manufacture a write revision. This does not skip active camera producers or claim GPU completion.

**Why:** attachment capability alone forced repeated capture rasterization even between camera writes. **Verify:** CAPTURE-WRITE-VERIFY in Overhaul.md owns static/animated previews, first completion, inactive/active transitions, multiple writers, producer removal, replacement/resize, CPU uploads, private/public aliases and missing assets/pipelines. Compare fingerprint/registry CPU and allocations with encoded/reused pass counts and total input/resource cost. Require fresh pixels, privacy and existing wake/order behavior. The new batch is unbuilt, untested and unmeasured; broader producer scheduling remains conditional, not another required implementation under this task.

} r_4MPVWB5R7J40MNV571W780DQ9W

